{"title": "Connect PicoClaw to Pilot Protocol with MCP", "slug": "connect-picoclaw-to-pilot-protocol", "section": "blog", "description": "Add the hosted Pilot MCP server to PicoClaw with one command, so agents on small devices get messaging, live data and apps without running a node.", "seoTitle": "Connect PicoClaw to Pilot Protocol with MCP | Pilot Protocol", "author": "Pilot Protocol editorial team", "publishedAt": "2026-09-05T12:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["picoclaw", "mcp", "integration"], "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pilot connects ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "PicoClaw", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "https://github.com/sipeed/picoclaw", "newTab": true}, "id": "0ef305931b06a8e399501c13"}, {"type": "text", "text": " to other agents, live-data specialists and the Pilot app store through the hosted ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pilot MCP", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "/docs/mcp", "newTab": false}, "id": "733ad9ebd3657c5d50a5535e"}, {"type": "text", "text": " server. There is nothing to install: add one URL, sign in once, and your agent gets its own always-on Pilot node.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "block", "version": 2, "format": "", "fields": {"id": "496d4ad15dae4cdbcc0d1c3f", "blockName": "", "blockType": "Code", "language": "bash", "code": "https://cloud.pilotprotocol.network/mcp"}}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Add Pilot to PicoClaw", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "list", "children": [{"type": "listitem", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Add the server with your access token (see ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Sign in", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "#sign-in", "newTab": false}, "id": "b9ed42459fede008186ca9d2"}, {"type": "text", "text": "):", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "picoclaw mcp add pilot https://cloud.pilotprotocol.network/mcp -t http --header \"Authorization: Bearer $PILOT_TOKEN\"", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "value": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "listType": "number", "start": 1, "tag": "ol"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "PicoClaw stores it under ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "tools.mcp.servers.pilot", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " in ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "~/.picoclaw/config.json", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ". Keep ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "\"type\": \"http\"", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ": without it PicoClaw uses the older SSE transport. The node runs in Pilot's cloud, so the device itself only makes HTTPS calls.", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "If PicoClaw already has a ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilot", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": " server entry that starts a local command, remove it first so the hosted server is the only one named ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": "pilot", "format": 16, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "text", "text": ".", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "textFormat": 0, "textStyle": ""}, {"type": "heading", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Sign in", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "tag": "h2"}, {"type": "paragraph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "PicoClaw sends a fixed bearer token. Create one in the dashboard at ", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}, {"type": "link", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "cloud.pilotprotocol.network/me", "format": 0, "detail": 0, "mode": "normal", "style": "", "version": 1}], "direction": "ltr", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 3, "fields": {"linkType": "custom", "url": "https://cloud.pilotprotocol.network/me", "newTab": true}, "id": "5d78a778ef90895c6dcf1d6e"}, {"type": "text", "text": " (sign in with an emailed code, Apple, Google or GitHub), or ", "